Write a NUT clip instead of failing video output on Linux

The whole mp4 and mov muxer sits inside one canImport(AVFoundation) block, so
generate --output clip.mp4 hard-errors off Darwin, and the suggested PNG
fallback silently drops the audio tensor. The #else now writes a single
clip.nut holding rgb48le video, pcm_f32le stereo audio, and an info packet
carrying the prompt, model, seed, and the originally requested filename and
codec. ffmpeg, ffplay and mpv read it directly. NutMuxer compiles
unconditionally so a macOS build still type-checks it.
